# Grain.
#
# The other finishing style. Monochrome by default: coloured noise reads as a
# broken sensor, while grain in luminance alone reads as film.
#
# Scaled to nothing — grain is a property of the emulsion, not the enlargement,
# so it stays the same size in pixels however large the image is. That is the
# one place where not scaling with the document is the correct answer.

param amount = 0.05

filter add-noise amount={amount} monochromatic
